cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use VANE in academic work, please cite this software entry with the
  version you used.
title: "VANE: Visualization and Automated Natural-frequency Extraction"
type: software
abstract: >-
  VANE is an open-source Python package for the linearized dynamics of wind
  turbines modelled in OpenFAST. It runs OpenFAST linearization sweeps over a
  turbine's operating curve, applies the multi-blade coordinate transform,
  identifies and labels the modes from their physical participation, tracks
  them across operating points into Campbell diagrams with resonance
  crossings, estimates the error of the azimuth-averaged model, and exports
  state-space and linear parameter-varying models for estimator and
  controller design, for fixed-bottom and floating turbines.
